      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hickory Hill was incorporated as a home rule-class city on January 31, 1979, during a period of rapid suburban growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hickory_hill_kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hickory Hill is one of the tiniest municipalities in Jefferson County, covering only about zero point zero three square miles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hickory_hill_kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hickory Hill maintains a quiet, residential character as an affluent suburb about eleven miles east of downtown Louisville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hickory_hill_kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hickory Hill integrated into the broader Louisville and Jefferson County Metro Government following a merger in 2003.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
